  "title": "# Hire agents to own recurring jobs (Brett, Nov 1 ~3 AM) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES…",
  "asked": "# Hire agents to own recurring jobs (Brett, Nov 1 ~3 AM) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md, _claude/persona.md and the agent swarm on main (apps/console-web/plugins/agent-swarm + README + _claude/builds/reports/agent-swarm-2026-10-31.md + install_steps Part I). Opus, one session. Git login works: plain `git push`. NOTE: the HR department (fun rules, raises, school, HR panel) is SHELVED (axHub data plans/shelved-hr-department.md). Do NOT build any of it. Use only what the swarm already has: hiring, specialties, statuses, salaries/token budgets, ID cards, group chat, leases. Brett: when Claude does recurring kinds of work (walkthrough videos, site checks, screenshots, landing builds, banner cleanup...), it should HIRE AGENTS to run that kind of stuff instead of spinning up anonymous one-off builds. 1. Job types as assets (job-type@1 in framework/schemas + validators): id, name, description, which specialty owns it, default model (sonnet for checks/routine, opus for building), token budget per run, trigger (on demand, schedule, event), brief template, outputs (report path, UI Review group naming). 2. Hire the first crew (real swarm agents with ID cards, specialties, salaries; work-only Amber-style catchphrases): - Walkthrough producer: makes and re-records app walkthrough videos (owns the amberx-walkthrough job; take over its outputs/re-record command when that build lands). - Site checker: read-only health checks of sites/apps on the VPS (demo.amberxai.com, axHub, console, AmberX web): route, HTTP, cert, container health, errors. - Screenshot runner: UI Review screenshots in named, timestamped groups (schema). - Lander: lands finished builds (vps build_land behaviour), resolves bookkeeping clashes, reports code clashes. - Banner janitor: ghosts, stuck lines, hook health. - Listener fixer / QA: voice + listener regressions in AmberX. 3. Routing: one entry point (CLI `node framework/cli/agent-job.mjs <job-type> --input ...` + console button + a short section in RULES.md telling Claude sessions to use it): picks the owning agent, checks it's on duty and under budget, writes the brief from the template, launches through deploy/claude-headless.sh (so the agent cap/queue applies when it lands) with the session named after the agent + job, and records the run on the agent's history/stats/cost. If no agent owns a job type, the Breakroom shows 'unassigned job' with a one-tap hire. 4. Breakroom: a Jobs view (job types, owner, last run, next scheduled, cost) and each agent's card shows its jobs. 5. Cost rule: agents get only their job's brief + their own short notes; nothing else loaded by default. Framework controls + theme/scale tokens only. Tests: job-type validation, routing to the owner, unassigned job path, budget check, run recorded on agent history, launcher naming. Local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle/menu-reach checks. Phone + desktop screenshots to UI Review via framework/cli/shot.mjs, group 'Agent jobs - Nov 1'. Add 'Part J: Jobs and the crew' to install_steps (or the next free letter; Part J was reserved for the shelved HR). Merge origin/main first (agent-cap, help-mode, banner-fix may land). Commit, fetch+merge origin/main, retest, `git push origin HEAD:main` (never force). Report at _claude/builds/reports/agent-jobs.md with the crew list. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault).",
